{
  "dom_id": "step-q86453",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{4|x|}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
  "worked_solution": "We break up the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{4|x|}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{4|x|}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{4|x|}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by calculating the second of these integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{4|x|}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{4x}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the antiderivative using a substitution. Let $u=1+{x}^{2}$,  then $\\text{d}u=2x\\text{d}x.$ Hence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4x}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2}{{u}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{2}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{4|x|}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{4x}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\frac{4x}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({-\\frac{1}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{2}}|}_{0}^{a}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(-\\frac{1}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{(1+0)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-0+1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the integrand $\\frac{4|x|}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{3}}$ is an **even** function. This means that we can immediately deduce that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{4|x|}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since both improper integrals exist, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{4|x|}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{4|x|}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{4|x|}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
